# Cloudflare Pages rewrites — keeps the original extensionless URLs working
# (/contact, /projects, ...) now that the files live in /pages/.
#
# Format:  <source>  <destination>  <code>
#   200 = rewrite (proxy). The visitor's URL bar keeps showing /contact,
#         so the existing canonical tags and sitemap.xml stay valid.
#
# !! Do NOT replace this list with a blanket  /*  /pages/:splat  200  rule.
#    On Cloudflare Pages redirects take precedence over static assets and
#    are followed even when a real file matches, so /*  would hijack
#    /css/style.css, /images/*, /js/main.js, /sitemap.xml and the homepage.
#
# Destination is the extension-less path (not .html) on purpose: Pages
# 301-redirects *.html to its extension-less form, so pointing a 200
# rewrite at a .html path can surface that redirect instead of the page.

